inishRateRank":67,"winningTimeRank":43,"winningTimeRankDir":24,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1952,"mensWinner":"Trevor ALLEN","mensTime":"07:00:02"}},"narrative":"The 1993 Comrades Marathon was the 68th running of the race, run in the 'down' direction from Pietermaritzburg to Durban over 89.900 km. The race was held on Monday, 31 May. Conditions: Clear day. Mild to warm. Runners had 11 hours to complete the course.\n\nCharly DOLL claimed the men's title in 05:39:41, ahead of Theo RAFIRI (05:42:16) and Mohala MOHLOLI (05:42:41). Tilda TEARLE won the women's race in 06:55:07, followed by Rae BISSCHOFF (07:00:30).\n\nTilda TEARLE's 06:55:07 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1952 (Trevor ALLEN, 07:00:02).\n\nFrom a field of 13,590 entries, 11,316 runners crossed the finish line (83.3% completion rate), with athletes representing over 19 countries. The field comprised 10,215 men and 1,101 women (9.7% female). The average finish time was 09:30:30.\n\nMedals awarded: 13 Gold, 989 Silver, 10,314 Bronze. 2,981 runners (26.3%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Paul NAIDOO in 10:59:59.\n\nCompared to the previous down run in 1991, the field was 9.5% smaller.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 31% of the finishers, with 7,806 seniors (avg 09:25:39) and 3,509 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}